        "text": "Subsecciones de: Chapter 6: Working with Disks and Filesystems\nP\u00e1ginas: 208-235\n\u2022 Technical requirements  (208)\n\u2022 Understanding devices in Linux  (208)\n  \u2022 Linux abstraction layers  (209)\n  \u2022 Device files and naming conventions  (210)\n\u2022 Understanding filesystem types in Linux  (213)\n\u2022 Understanding disks and partitions  (216)\n  \u2022 Common disk types  (216)\n  \u2022 Partitioning disks  (218)\n\u2022 Introducing LVM in Linux  (229)\n  \u2022 LVM snapshots  (232)\n\u2022 Summary  (234)\n\u2022 Questions  (235)\n\u2022 Further reading  (235)\n6\nWorking with Disks and\nFilesystems\nIn this chapter, you will learn how to manage disks and filesystems, how to use the Logical Volume\nManagement ( LVM ) system, and how to mount and partition the hard drive, as well as gain an\nunderstanding of storage in Linux. You will also learn how to partition and format a disk, as well as\nhow to create logical volumes, and you will gain a deeper understanding of filesystem types. In this\nchapter, we\u2019re going to cover the following main topics:\n\u2022I Understanding devices in Linux\n\u2022I Understanding filesystem types in Linux\n\u2022I Understanding disks and partitions\n\u2022I Introducing LVM in Linux",
